# gitleaks per-finding baseline for agent-skills.
#
# .gitleaks.toml forbids path-wide allowlists on purpose: a path exemption
# would blind the FULL-HISTORY scan to a credential that once lived in that
# file. Its stated escape hatch is exactly this file — a fingerprint per
# finding, each with an explanation, reviewed like any other change.
#
# All five entries below are SYNTHETIC FIXTURES for the handoff gate's own
# regression suite (skills/handoff/scripts/test-handoff-gate.sh). The gate is
# a credential detector; its tests must feed it credential-shaped strings, and
# each of these was invented for that test — none is, or ever was, a real
# credential for any account.
#
# They are listed here only because gitleaks scans history and these commits
# are already pushed. At the tip of this branch the suite builds every fake
# secret at RUNTIME (string concatenation), so no credential-shaped literal
# is committed any more and no new fingerprint is needed for future commits.

